  <prompt>
    UAT round 3 (`notes/UAT-ROUND3-FEEDBACK.md` section A) refinements to the `CommunicationAttachments` PCF
    (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationAttachments/`). Five items:

    A11-1 (BUG) — the preview modal shows a DOUBLE header (the file title renders twice; see feedback). Root-cause it:
    compare EXACTLY how `SemanticSearchControl` mounts `RichFilePreviewDialog` (does it pass a title/header prop AND
    also render its own header?) vs how CommunicationAttachments mounts it. Make CommunicationAttachments mount the
    dialog the SAME way SemanticSearchControl does so only ONE title header renders. Do not fork the dialog.

    A11-2 + A11-3 — replace the LEFT per-row file-type glyph with an UPLOAD-STATUS icon: a SharePoint icon in green
    when the attachment's document has an uploaded SPE file, red when it does not. Determine "uploaded" from the
    attachment/document data already available to the control (inspect the `sprk_communicationattachment` /
    `sprk_document` fields the control already reads — e.g. a has-file / drive-item-id / graph-item-id field; do NOT
    add a new BFF call). KEEP the right-side type pill (PDF / Email / DOCX) as-is.

    A11-4 — make the section title a PCF PROPERTY (bound or input property in the manifest), defaulting to
    "ATTACHMENTS". The host reads the property and renders it as the title.

    A11-5 — render that title in ALL CAPS using the Spaarke OOB title spec from
    `docs/standards/UI-DESIGN-STANDARDS.md`: `tokens.fontSizeBase300` (14px) + `tokens.fontWeightSemibold` (600) +
    `tokens.colorNeutralForeground1` (#242424), 20px height, 4px top/bottom padding (`tokens.spacingVerticalXS`).
    Tokens only (ADR-021) — theme-correct light + dark.
  </prompt>

  <goal>
    The attachment preview shows a single title header (mounted like SemanticSearchControl); each row shows a
    green/red SharePoint upload-status icon in the left slot (type pill kept on the right); the section title is a
    configurable PCF property defaulting to "ATTACHMENTS", rendered ALL CAPS in the OOB title token spec.
  </goal>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The preview modal renders the file title ONCE (double-header gone); the mount matches SemanticSearchControl's RichFilePreviewDialog usage (documented in a code comment or the task notes with the specific prop/wrapper difference that caused the duplication).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each attachment row's LEFT icon is a SharePoint glyph: green when the row's document has an uploaded SPE file, red when not — derived from existing attachment/document fields (no new BFF endpoint). The right-side type pill (PDF/Email/DOCX) is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A manifest property controls the section title, default "ATTACHMENTS"; changing the property changes the rendered title. (State whether bound or input and why.)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The title renders ALL CAPS via `fontSizeBase300` + `fontWeightSemibold` + `colorNeutralForeground1` + 20px height + 4px vertical padding tokens (no hardcoded hex/px); legible in dark theme.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` clean; jest updated/green (add a test for the upload-status mapping + title-prop default); version bump all 5 locations (1.1.0 → 1.2.0); solution ZIP repacked + validated (type-66, manifest generic + apostrophe-free per R2 XSD fix).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">§11: reuse RichFilePreviewDialog (no new modal), no new BFF surface; upload status read from existing data.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>ADR-021 Fluent v9 tokens only; ADR-022 platform libs / virtual control; ADR-028 auth unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint>Do NOT fork or copy RichFilePreviewDialog — fix the mount to match SemanticSearchControl.</constraint>
    <constraint>Do NOT add a BFF call for upload status — use fields the control already loads. If genuinely unavailable, STOP and report rather than adding a new endpoint.</constraint>
